    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nPreserve explicitly configured MFSDP v2 sharding policies instead of overwriting non-expert inner sharding with `optim_grads_params`. For example, DeepSeek V3 MLPerf requests non-expert inner `optim_grads`, expert inner `optim_grads_params`, and `optim` on both outer axes; validation now keeps that combination intact.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- Remove the forced non-expert ZeRO-3 override; retain the dedicated v2 optimizer settings and existing unsupported-feature guards.\n- Add configuration tests for independent expert/non-expert policies and inheritance of unset expert policies.\n- Document the 256-GPU/EP64 layout: non-expert `(outer=4, inner=64)` and expert `(outer=4, inner=1)` meshes.\n\n# Dependency\n\nRequires the companion MCore adapter fix https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/7728, which depends on DBuffer support in https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/7633. The adapter PR removes the v2 ZeRO-3-only guard; the DBuffer PR gathers replicated model weights from optimizer shards across both axes. This PR does not change the MCore submodule pin.\n\n# Validation\n\n- 15 FSDP configuration tests passed in `tests/unit_tests/training/test_config.py`.\n- Both v1 and v2 full BF16 MLPerf configuration dry runs preserved all four requested sharding policies with the patched MCore sources.\n- `uv run pre-commit run --all-files`: passed.\n- Before the MCore split, with combined MCore #7633 and cleanup #7662, the 0.3B DeepSeek V3 MLA/MoE proxy completed 20 steps on eight EOS H100s for both dense `(2,4)` / expert `(2,2)` and dense `(4,2)` / expert `(4,1)` meshes. Both runs preserved all four requested policies, used BF16 with training/optimizer CUDA graphs, and had no skipped or NaN iterations. Loss fell from `10.58813` to `5.40518` / `5.405465`. Runtime: PyTorch `2.14.0a0+4fdf77b940.nv26.08`, Transformer Engine `2.19.0+5e52befd`.\n\nThe companion MCore change passed the eight-GPU DBuffer suite, FP32/BF16 optimizer reconstruction checks, and all 39 adapter tests per rank. Full 256-GPU training remains unverified. FP8 and checkpointing remain unsupported by this Bridge v2 path.\n\n# Before your PR is ready for review\n\n- [x] Followed the contributor guidelines.\n- [x] Added relevant tests.\n- [x] Updated documentation.\n- [ ] Companion MCore fix is available in the pinned dependency.\n",
